    "result_text": "Full build succeeds. The change is complete:\n\n- **New `OwnerTimezone` class** \u2014 a single tiny static `of(owner)` method (CC 1, no surrounding class complexity) that reads the region via the existing `OwnerLocality.region(owner)` and maps it through the fixed table `NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane` (any other region \u2192 `null`, so the field is absent).\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line for `timezone`, mirroring the existing `locality` mapping.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 a `timezone` read-only string property so the generated DTO carries the field.\n\nStructural impact stays low: the new logic lives in its own cohesive unit with zero `WMC_other`, the mapper edit is a single line on a CC-1 method, and no existing function grew in complexity. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
